# Install scripts stay off for this package.
#
# Exactly one package in the tree declares a hook: esbuild@0.28.2 (MIT),
# `postinstall: node install.js`, pulled in by Vite. install.js validates the
# platform binary and hard-links it over `bin/esbuild`; it does not download
# anything when the optional dependency below is present. That binary arrives
# as a real file from `@esbuild/linux-x64` (an optionalDependency installed by
# npm, not a script), and esbuild's JS API — which Vite uses — resolves the
# binary from that package, not from `bin/esbuild`.
#
# So the hook is redundant for this build, and it is the only one: every other
# package.json under node_modules has no preinstall/install/postinstall.
#
# Proven cold, not warm: `rm -rf node_modules && npm ci && npm run check`
# passes with this file in place (README § Install scripts records the run).
ignore-scripts=true
